  JOURNAL   Cell 53 (2), 219-228 (1988)
   PUBMED   3282674
COMMENT     REVIEWED REFSEQ: This record has been curated by NCBI staff in
            collaboration with Johan den Dunnen. The reference sequence was
            derived from AL050305.9, AL031643.1, AL049643.12, AL139401.14,
            AL451144.5, AL121880.21, AL096699.11, AC004468.1, AL596023.2,
            AL031542.1, AL109609.5, AL139278.12, AC096506.5, AC078957.16,
            AC093193.11, AC079864.22, AC093167.11, AC079175.24, AC079177.21,
            AC090632.13, AC078958.30, AC079143.17 and AC006061.1.
            This sequence is a reference standard in the RefSeqGene project.
            
            Summary: This gene spans a genomic range of greater than 2 Mb and
            encodes a large protein containing an N-terminal actin-binding
            domain and multiple spectrin repeats. The encoded protein forms a
            component of the dystrophin-glycoprotein complex (DGC), which
            bridges the inner cytoskeleton and the extracellular matrix.
            Deletions, duplications, and point mutations at this gene locus may
            cause Duchenne muscular dystrophy (DMD), Becker muscular dystrophy
            (BMD), or cardiomyopathy. Alternative promoter usage and
            alternative splicing result in numerous distinct transcript
            variants and protein isoforms for this gene. [provided by RefSeq,
            Dec 2016].
